I believe this is bug C343-151: "Monsters can teleport to or be
created outside of legal area in special levels."

It's been a long time since I looked at that part of the code, but I
seem to recall the issue was that the squares outside the actual area
of the level are filled with rock which is marked undiggable, but not
unphasable.  So the monster placement code may consider those squares
valid locations for phasing monsters like xorns.  If the actual walls
of the level are unphasable, this means that those monsters are stuck
outside the walls.

This is most likely to happen if the interior of the level is already
full of monsters, or if the level is unusually small (like Sokoban).
I suspect the only reason it's not seen more often in Soko is that
phasing monsters are unlikely to be randomly generated that high in
the dungeon at the XL most players have when they do that branch.

In principle, you should be able to polymorph yourself into a phasing
monster, teleport outside the walls and either kill or teleport the
monsters stuck there.  Alas, most (if not all) levels with unphasable
walls are also no-teleport.  I suppose taming the monsters (with a
confused scroll of taming) and then whistling them out of the wall
with a magic whistle might work, though I haven't tested it.

